    "The scalar energy identity at e.symm f, followed by the actual59 defect identity and isometry norm preservation, gives norm(ΓP f)²=norm(f)²-norm(Af)² for every f. The typed Gram identity plus positivity/selfadjointness of ΓP equates norm(Bf)² and norm(ΓP f)²; nonnegative norms justify the unsquared equality.",
    "For ANY positive G:HP→L[ℝ]HP with G²=I_HP-A², inverse conjugation gives positive G0=e.symm.conj G with G0²=I_scalar-T². Generic62 positive_square_roots_unique applies to G0 and Γ on L2(ν). Conjugating back proves G=ΓP. The competing-root quantifier is outside the forall-f energy conjunct and requires no alternative energy, CFC, commutation or supplied root certificate.",
